{"title":"Career roadmap — Pollution Control Officer","role":"Pollution Control Officer","summary":"A Pollution Control Officer is responsible for monitoring, controlling, and reducing environmental pollution from industrial, municipal, infrastructure, and commercial activities. The role covers air pollution, water pollution, wastewater, solid and hazardous waste, environmental monitoring, compliance, inspections, environmental audits, and pollution-control technologies.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Environmental Engineering"},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"★★★★★ — Environmental Engineering provides one of the strongest academic pathways for this career."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build environmental science, pollution-control, laboratory and regulatory fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Enter as Environmental Engineer / Pollution Control Officer / EHS Executive"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Environmental Engineer / Environmental Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead environmental compliance, sustainability, pollution prevention and environmental risk programmes"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Chemistry, biology, mathematics, physics, environmental science"},{"text":"Basic laboratory analysis and environmental sampling"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Water treatment, wastewater engineering, air pollution, solid waste"},{"text":"Water/air-quality experiments and treatment-system visits"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Industrial pollution control, hazardous waste, environmental monitoring, EIA"},{"text":"Industrial environmental internship and compl